---
title: Frame scheduler
description: Register per-frame tasks, invalidation policies, and ordering dependencies.
---

`useFrame(...)` registers a callback in the `FragCanvas` scheduler. It must run inside the canvas subtree and automatically unregisters through the adapter lifecycle.

## Signatures

```ts
useFrame(callback, options?)
useFrame(key, callback, options?)
```

An explicit string or symbol key makes ordering and diagnostic output stable. Registering the same explicit key again replaces the previous task; a stale cleanup from the old registration cannot remove the replacement.

## Frame state

| Member | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `time`, `delta` | RAF time in seconds and delta clamped by `maxDelta` |
| `canvas` | Active canvas element |
| `renderMode`, `autoRender` | Current render-gate state |
| `setUniform`, `setTexture` | Set runtime resource overrides |
| `writeStorageBuffer` | Queue an owned copy of an aligned CPU-to-GPU write |
| `readStorageBuffer` | Flush that buffer's queued writes, then read it asynchronously |
| `invalidate`, `advance` | Request on-demand or manual rendering |

## Options

| Option | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `autoStart` | `true` | Start the task immediately |
| `autoInvalidate` | `true` | Use implicit `'always'` invalidation |
| `invalidation` | Implicit | Explicit `'never'`, `'always'`, or token policy |
| `stage` | Main stage | Stage key or `FrameStage` |
| `before`, `after` | — | Task dependencies in the same stage |
| `running` | — | Dynamic predicate checked every frame |

The returned handle contains task metadata, `start()`, `stop()`, and a `started: Subscribable<boolean>` flag. Stopping a task keeps it registered but skips its callback.

## Invalidation policies

```ts
useFrame('sync-data', syncData, {
	invalidation: {
		mode: 'on-change',
		token: () => dataVersion
	}
});
```

- `'always'` invalidates whenever the task runs.
- `'never'` does not invalidate.
- `{ mode: 'on-change', token }` compares the resolved string, number, or symbol token with the previous run.
- `{ mode: 'always', token }` invalidates with the supplied static or resolved token.

An `on-change` policy requires a token. The first non-null resolved token and every subsequent changed token invalidate the frame. Resolving `null` or `undefined` clears the stored comparison state.

## Ordering

```ts
const simulation = useFrame('simulation', updateSimulation);

useFrame('upload', uploadState, {
	after: simulation.task
});
```

`before` and `after` accept task keys, task metadata, or arrays of either. Dependencies order tasks within a stage. If a task omits `stage`, the registry uses the stage of the first task-metadata dependency it finds; otherwise it uses the main stage. References to known tasks in other stages do not create cross-stage ordering—order those stages separately.

Use [Render Modes](/docs/render-modes) for render gating, stages, and profiling. Runtime resource rules are documented under [Uniforms](/docs/uniforms), [Textures](/docs/textures), and [Storage Buffers](/docs/storage-buffers).
